    <string name="science_topic7_title">7. Kinetic Destruction vs. Human Metabolic kJ</string>
    <string name="science_topic7_desc">Every brake event destroys kinetic energy (1/2·m·Δv²). At human gross efficiency (~21.5%), recovering 15 kJ of lost momentum requires burning nearly 70 kJ of muscle glycogen. Minimizing hesitation preserves aerobic reserves for key climbs.</string>
    <string name="science_topic8_title">8. Peloton Accordion Waves &amp; Position Index</string>
    <string name="science_topic8_desc">Micro-braking at the front of a paceline amplifies backward into a non-linear accordion shockwave. Riders trailing in positions 50-80 face repeated zero-braking to 800W sprints. The Peloton Smoothness Index (PEI) measures draft fluidity to coach energy preservation.</string>

